# Trivy ignore list — entries here are tracked in CLAUDE.md "Upgrade Backlog".
# Remove an entry once the corresponding backlog item ships.

# (Currently empty — no active waivers.)
#
# 2026-07-29: the three alpine OS-package waivers that lived here (CVE-2026-45447
# openssl, CVE-2026-45186 libexpat, CVE-2026-6732 libxml2) expired on 2026-07-22
# and were REMOVED as dead rather than re-dated. Measured on 2026-07-29 with the
# waivers explicitly disabled (`trivy image --ignorefile /dev/null`):
#   * caddy:2.11.4-alpine now resolves to alpine 3.23.5 with libcrypto3/libssl3
#     3.5.7-r0, and `apk upgrade --simulate` offers nothing newer for them —
#     i.e. openssl is already patched upstream, not merely unfixed.
#   * libexpat and libxml2 are NOT INSTALLED in this image at all.
#   * All three CVE IDs return ZERO hits against both the base image and the
#     built prod image.
# The five alpine CVEs the base image DOES still carry (c-ares CVE-2026-33630,
# curl/libcurl CVE-2026-5773 + CVE-2026-6276) are all fixed-in-repo and are
# cleared by Dockerfile.prod's `apk --no-cache upgrade` — the built image scans
# 0 on the alpine layer, so they need no waiver either.
#
# House style for any future entry: state (a) why it is unpatchable upstream,
# (b) the reachability analysis, (c) the auto-remediation path, and (d) an
# `exp:` date so the waiver expires and forces re-evaluation. Track each one in
# the CLAUDE.md "Upgrade Backlog".
